    "lawCode": "Amd §203, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8689\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the elder law, in relation to authorizing the office for\nthe aging to establish, operate and maintain programs for transportation\nservices\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires NYSOFA to establish, operate and maintain programs for trans-\nportation services.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the Elder Law to require NYSOFA to establish, operate and main-\ntain programs for transportation services.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOne of the top needs for Older New Yorkers throughout New York State is\ntransportation, including for medical, social and wellness purposes. It\nis high time to update the Elder Law to recognize this reality.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n30 Days.\n",
